1
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,719
Mr. Fang!

2
00:01:53,799 --> 00:01:54,640
Mr. Fang!

3
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,920
Dantian, Dantian, Dantian.

4
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:58,200
He's awake.

5
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,040
Are you hungry? Are you cold?

6
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,439
Do you feel uncomfortable anywhere?

7
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,639
Mr. Fang, why are you sleeping on the floor?

8
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,919
Well, this bed is too soft.

9
00:02:13,919 --> 00:02:15,159
It's uncomfortable to sleep on.

10
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,000
One for each of us.

11
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,599
I don't smoke.

12
00:02:22,599 --> 00:02:24,599
Mr. Fang, a lighter is no use to me.

13
00:02:24,599 --> 00:02:25,879
A lighter is one of those things...

14
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:26,759
that seems useless,

15
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,520
but when you need it and don't have it,

16
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,439
it's really frustrating.

17
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,000
I bought this ages ago.

18
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:40,199
I've been waiting for you.

19
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,199
Didn't dare touch it. Saved it just for you.

20
00:02:44,639 --> 00:02:45,120
Dig in.

21
00:02:48,719 --> 00:02:49,400
Oh my god.

22
00:02:49,479 --> 00:02:50,439
Tastes like heaven, doesn't it?

23
00:02:50,439 --> 00:02:51,479
Tastes like heaven, doesn't it?

24
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:55,800
So good.

25
00:02:58,439 --> 00:02:59,120
A bit dry, right?

26
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,479
This is true art. What is art?

27
00:03:06,479 --> 00:03:07,199
This is art.

28
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:10,240
So, Mr. Fang,

29
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,759
how did we get here?

30
00:03:12,879 --> 00:03:13,960
You've been out for a day.

31
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,680
I was out that long?

32
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,240
The doctor gave you an anti-inflammatory shot.

33
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,639
Your leg will be fine by tomorrow.

34
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,879
Mr. Fang.

35
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,439
The cup Rong Sihai gave me...

36
00:03:25,439 --> 00:03:26,400
I left it in the cave.

37
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,360
The books you gave me all burned, too. It's a shame.

38
00:03:30,159 --> 00:03:31,199
I'll buy you a new cup.

39
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,039
I didn't burn all the books.

40
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,960
Don't be afraid of failure

41
00:03:47,039 --> 00:03:48,479
There's always hope

42
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,159
"What is Success"

43
00:03:50,159 --> 00:03:51,319
By Fang Haowen

44
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,879
Don't mind what others think

45
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:56,319
You're actually not stupid at all

46
00:03:56,639 --> 00:03:58,080
Wishing you a baby soon

47
00:03:58,159 --> 00:03:59,800
Your close friend, Fang Haowen

48
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,639
Why are there two extra lines?

49
00:04:01,639 --> 00:04:02,840
I just wrote this new part.

50
00:04:04,599 --> 00:04:05,719
And let me tell you,

51
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,039
I didn't write the first part.

52
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,159
Mr. Fang.

53
00:04:11,479 --> 00:04:12,120
Mr. Fang.

54
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,639
Hey, let's wait in line.

55
00:04:14,439 --> 00:04:15,199
Here's the thing.

56
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,199
My son is a bit special.

57
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,560
I'd like to ask Mr. Fang

58
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,600
to write him a few more encouraging words.

59
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,839
That's your son?

60
00:04:23,079 --> 00:04:24,879
Growing up to be this big is already a huge success for your son.

61
00:04:24,879 --> 00:04:26,040
Stop keeping Mr. Fang

62
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:26,920
from inspiring everyone else.

63
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,279
So many people are waiting to be inspired.

64
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,480
No, uh...

65
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,680
Just... go back.

66
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,560
All signed.

67
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,319
Thank you, Mr. Fang.

68
00:04:45,199 --> 00:04:45,879
Borrowing this.

69
00:04:47,439 --> 00:04:48,399
Why are you taking my pen?

70
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:02,519
Thank you.

71
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:05,680
Son.

72
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,240
Mr. Fang signed it for you.

73
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,759
Take a look.

74
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,279
That's a big win, right?

75
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,399
Don't be afraid.

76
00:05:20,959 --> 00:05:24,079
Failure hope will always be there.

77
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,839
You need to watch your phrasing.

78
00:05:26,399 --> 00:05:27,879
Don't be afraid of failure.

79
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,279
Hope is always there.

80
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:33,240
Mr. Fang.

81
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,600
Thank you, Mr. Fang.

82
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,319
You're a good guy.

83
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,360
Eat up.

84
00:05:48,439 --> 00:05:49,759
I'll take you to the police station later.

85
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:51,040
And then we'll take a walk around Tiananmen.

86
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,319
Okay.

87
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,480
You're awake.

88
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:56,879
Bie Fan.

89
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,000
Bie Fan!

90
00:05:59,240 --> 00:05:59,959
Sihai!

91
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,279
How come you're awake?

92
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,720
You... why are you here?

93
00:06:07,279 --> 00:06:09,120
I've been waiting for you all day.

94
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,160
I just went down for some fruit and you woke up.

95
00:06:12,199 --> 00:06:13,519
I've been looking for you for two months.

96
00:06:13,759 --> 00:06:15,079
You even made it on TV.

97
00:06:16,079 --> 00:06:18,040
You looked for me for two months?

98
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,560
Then what did you even eat?

99
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,560
Food, obviously.

100
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:22,240
I know.

101
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,759
I figured. I just knew.

102
00:06:23,759 --> 00:06:25,399
I knew you'd look for me. Given our bond.

103
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,079
Given our bond.

104
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,079
Hurry, Sihai.

105
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:32,959
Have a seat, have a seat.

106
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:33,399
Okay.

107
00:06:33,399 --> 00:06:34,639
Make yourself at home.

108
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,360
Okay.

109
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,759
I miss your cooking.

110
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:41,160
Don't even mention it.

111
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,639
I miss your cooking too.

112
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,879
When you were gone,

113
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:45,480
my cooking always felt like...

114
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,040
Wang Yue.

115
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,800
I can't put my finger on it.

116
00:06:58,839 --> 00:07:00,120
I knew you'd come looking for me.

117
00:07:01,319 --> 00:07:02,639
You've been looking for over two months, huh?

118
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,120
Oh my god.

119
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,040
Wait, if you're looking for me, what about your husband?

120
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:07,800
Where is your husband?

121
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,279
Right here!

122
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:11,399
Who are you?

123
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,040
Fang Haowen!

124
00:07:18,399 --> 00:07:19,240
Haozi!

125
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,800
I knew you weren't dead!

126
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,680
Mr. Fang!

127
00:07:27,759 --> 00:07:28,519
What brings you here?

128
00:07:28,959 --> 00:07:30,000
We got here yesterday!

129
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,199
After we got married,

130
00:07:34,199 --> 00:07:36,680
we had to host a reception at Wang Yue's place, right?

131
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,480
We arrived yesterday.

132
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,399
The reception is tomorrow.

133
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:41,040
But she said her stomach felt a bit off,

134
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:41,639
so I got worried

135
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:42,959
and rushed her to the hospital

136
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:43,959
for a proper checkup.

137
00:07:44,279 --> 00:07:45,279
I didn't expect

138
00:07:46,319 --> 00:07:47,240
such a coincidence

139
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,759
to bump into our great matchmaker, Mr. Fang!

140
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,480
My hand! My hand's hurt! My hand!

141
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,560
No, no, no, my bad!

142
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:54,240
Are you okay?

143
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,240
Reception.

144
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,279
Arrived yesterday.

145
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,120
What a coincidence.

146
00:08:01,519 --> 00:08:02,240
Honey,

147
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,639
I'll go grab a smoke then.

148
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,519
You two catch up. Catch up.

149
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,319
Mr. Fang,

150
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:19,920
you really are...

151
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,240
so warmhearted.

152
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,240
Didn't you say

153
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,680
that writers who smoke

154
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,800
are empty-headed?

155
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,480
I don't smoke.

156
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:35,320
I just simply like fire.

157
00:08:36,639 --> 00:08:38,639
Seeing you here really is a coincidence, huh.

158
00:08:38,639 --> 00:08:39,639
Coincidence my ass.

159
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,080
I refused to believe you were dead.

160
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,440
I told Zhao En

161
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,440
to come back and see you.

162
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,519
Just in case you weren't dead.

163
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,840
Guess that "in case" came true, huh.

164
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:50,080
Sit.

165
00:09:00,919 --> 00:09:01,720
Seeing you

166
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,399
is so great. I'm absolutely ecstatic.

167
00:09:07,639 --> 00:09:08,919
Sorry, sorry! Does it hurt?

168
00:09:11,399 --> 00:09:12,039
I'm fine.

169
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:17,080
Alright, you're the educated one.

170
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,159
I can't eat anymore.

171
00:09:36,639 --> 00:09:37,360
I'm pregnant.

172
00:09:56,759 --> 00:09:57,480
I was wondering...

173
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:00,720
...if the baby and I...

174
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,279
With you?

175
00:10:04,519 --> 00:10:05,200
With me...

176
00:10:05,639 --> 00:10:06,559
What's it got to do with you?

177
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,200
...share the same zodiac sign?

178
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,600
Weren't you born in February?

179
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,080
This baby is due in August.

180
00:10:18,039 --> 00:10:20,679
Unbelievable. You held that in just to ask about zodiac signs?

181
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:28,600
One more thing.

182
00:10:30,559 --> 00:10:32,240
That night with Jin Furong...

183
00:10:32,519 --> 00:10:33,320
Nothing happened at all.

184
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,159
I haven't dated anyone else since you.

185
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,639
I know there's no point in saying this.

186
00:10:41,639 --> 00:10:43,440
But I just wanted to tell you, you know?

187
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,360
Okay.

188
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,000
Got it.

189
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,080
Thanks, I guess.

190
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,480
Well, at your age...

191
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,879
Shouldn't you find someone too?

192
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,200
You're not exactly a looker...

193
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,879
You're getting older...

194
00:11:03,799 --> 00:11:05,000
Your health probably isn't great...

195
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,440
And you have a bad temper.

196
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,519
Don't I have any good qualities?

197
00:11:10,759 --> 00:11:11,639
You're a decent person.

198
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,279
Nothing good about my looks?

199
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,279
You're a really decent person.

200
00:11:27,799 --> 00:11:28,919
Then set me up with someone.

201
00:11:30,039 --> 00:11:30,519
Okay.

202
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,320
I'll keep that in mind.

203
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,120
It's almost time.

204
00:11:52,519 --> 00:11:54,000
I'm gonna go see if he's done smoking.

205
00:11:55,039 --> 00:11:55,600
I'm off.

206
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:08,519
Yue'er.

207
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,440
Wishing you a happy marriage!

208
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,159
Wishing you happiness every day.

209
00:13:17,039 --> 00:13:18,000
Hello, excuse me.

210
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:18,879
Is there any hot water here?

211
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,480
There's a dispenser in the water room. Help yourself.

212
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:24,480
What book are you reading?

213
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,919
"I 'Have No' Talent"

214
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,120
Written by Fang Haowen.

215
00:13:30,919 --> 00:13:31,879
I haven't even published it yet.

216
00:13:32,519 --> 00:13:34,080
Just hit the shelves. Hard to find.

217
00:13:34,399 --> 00:13:35,360
You haven't read this book?

218
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,080
This guy is incredibly talented.

219
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,279
Just died too young.

220
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:39,320
He's dead?

221
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,039
Yeah, he's dead.

222
00:13:44,879 --> 00:13:46,080
So do you think the book is good?

223
00:13:46,519 --> 00:13:47,840
It's really deep.

224
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:48,799
Really hard to understand.

225
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,000
But it grows on you the more you read.

226
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:52,360
It's a poetry collection.

227
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:53,720
It's super interesting.

228
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,639
Such a shame.

229
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,120
Look at this Fang Haowen...

230
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,320
Blew up after he died.

231
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,559
Number one trending every day.

232
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,279
What do you mean, trending?

233
00:14:01,279 --> 00:14:02,200
Take a look. Number one.

234
00:14:02,399 --> 00:14:04,120
Tomorrow, Huanxi City will hold

235
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,679
a grand Fang Haowen

236
00:14:05,919 --> 00:14:06,799
memorial service.

237
00:14:15,639 --> 00:14:16,360
Why are you here?

238
00:14:18,519 --> 00:14:19,720
Fang.

239
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,720
I was worried something might happen to you.

240
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:24,200
So I came along with you.

241
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,080
Then why are you here?

242
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,399
I was worried something might happen to him.

243
00:14:29,399 --> 00:14:30,840
So I followed him here.

244
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,440
And why are you here?

245
00:14:35,639 --> 00:14:36,200
He's asking you.

246
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,639
Standing ticket. Just leaning to rest.

247
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,799
Mr. Fang, wait for me!

248
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:01,279
You're really talented.

249
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:02,440
Mr. Fang!

250
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,279
You were my pillar of strength!

251
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,679
Your sewer owes Fang Haowen an apology!

252
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:10,360
Your manhole cover hurt Mr. Fang!

253
00:15:10,519 --> 00:15:11,279
Excuse me.

254
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:12,960
Is this where Mr. Fang Haowen fell in?

255
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,840
I don't know where he fell in.

256
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,279
I just got transferred here.

257
00:15:16,279 --> 00:15:17,399
Alright, it's confirmed, guys.

258
00:15:17,399 --> 00:15:19,279
This is exactly where Mr. Fang Haowen fell in.

259
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,960
Come on, let's take a closer look.

260
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:24,080
Hi everyone, I'm Fang Haowen's landlord.

261
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:26,159
I know you all feel bad for him.

262
00:15:26,159 --> 00:15:27,960
But have some pity on me, too!

263
00:15:28,919 --> 00:15:31,320
Stop sending things, there's already so much!

264
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,279
The first week of mourning has already passed!

265
00:15:56,879 --> 00:15:57,879
My dearest Wen,

266
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:01,919
As I stand here today,

267
00:16:03,799 --> 00:16:06,360
my heart is immensely heavy and full of pain.

268
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,039
Yes,

269
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,039
I know you're gone,

270
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:14,879
but I still

271
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,960
can't believe it's real.

272
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,279
I remember when we first met.

273
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,039
In your eyes,

274
00:16:23,639 --> 00:16:25,919
there was a sorrow that didn't belong in this world.

275
00:16:27,759 --> 00:16:28,759
So quiet,

276
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,679
like an unfinished epic.

277
00:16:32,559 --> 00:16:33,759
Even though we once had

278
00:16:34,519 --> 00:16:35,799
our misunderstandings and arguments.

279
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:37,600
Even though you once chose to leave.

280
00:16:37,879 --> 00:16:39,679
I could never forget

281
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
the warmth you gave me.

282
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,240
Because,

283
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:48,320
I love you.

284
00:16:50,279 --> 00:16:51,159
I will keep you forever

285
00:16:51,159 --> 00:16:53,159
in the deepest part of my heart.

286
