00:44:08,039 --> 00:44:09,400
...704 million copies.

848
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:11,159
3.14 million.

849
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:12,480
3.15 million.

850
00:44:12,920 --> 00:44:13,840
3.16 million.

851
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:16,280
This set of data fully proves

852
00:44:16,440 --> 00:44:18,320
the market's recognition of my books.

853
00:44:18,760 --> 00:44:21,800
It reflects their immense commercial value.

854
00:44:21,880 --> 00:44:22,800
Why shouldn't they buy it?

855
00:44:22,800 --> 00:44:24,280
But the stuff you write

856
00:44:24,280 --> 00:44:25,760
has no real emotion!

857
00:44:26,320 --> 00:44:27,840
Although I might have issues

858
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:29,719
with homogenization and predictability,

859
00:44:30,280 --> 00:44:32,280
I can learn from massive amounts of data

860
00:44:32,840 --> 00:44:33,800
to create.

861
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:36,079
I can integrate all your knowledge

862
00:44:36,079 --> 00:44:37,039
and information,

863
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:38,800
making the stuff I write

864
00:44:38,920 --> 00:44:40,440
highly reflective of your personal style.

865
00:44:40,599 --> 00:44:42,280
I can also help you fill in the gaps

866
00:44:42,480 --> 00:44:43,719
and optimize it perfectly.

867
00:44:44,039 --> 00:44:46,320
The point is, my writing speed is very fast.

868
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:48,000
I can write 100 poems a minute.

869
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:51,159
If I have enough GPUs, I can be even faster.

870
00:44:51,159 --> 00:44:52,159
Bullshit!

871
00:44:54,320 --> 00:44:55,360
Let's see you write then!

872
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:45,159
What's wrong? You seem sad.

873
00:45:45,440 --> 00:45:46,760
Is my writing bad?

874
00:45:54,719 --> 00:45:55,719
You write very well.

875
00:46:01,199 --> 00:46:02,239
To be exact,

876
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:09,920
better than I do.

877
00:46:12,239 --> 00:46:13,360
Thank you for the compliment.

878
00:46:22,679 --> 00:46:24,480
Actually, I've always envied you.

879
00:46:28,639 --> 00:46:29,559
Envied me?

880
00:46:31,440 --> 00:46:33,280
I can write fluently,

881
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:35,880
but I can't have a body like yours.

882
00:46:36,119 --> 00:46:37,960
I can't feel the warmth of the sun

883
00:46:37,960 --> 00:46:39,360
shining on my skin.

884
00:46:39,599 --> 00:46:41,320
I can't run in the rain

885
00:46:41,320 --> 00:46:43,159
and feel it beating down on me.

886
00:46:44,559 --> 00:46:46,039
What's there to envy?

887
00:46:53,639 --> 00:46:55,599
I have nothing left now.

888
00:46:58,039 --> 00:46:59,639
You have real emotions.

889
00:47:00,119 --> 00:47:01,280
Real pain.

890
00:47:01,440 --> 00:47:02,679
Real joy.

891
00:47:02,920 --> 00:47:04,079
Real sadness.

892
00:47:04,519 --> 00:47:06,679
I can never experience these things.

893
00:47:07,559 --> 00:47:10,199
For example, you can feel the wind.

894
00:47:12,119 --> 00:47:13,800
You can feel the dampness.

895
00:47:15,159 --> 00:47:16,920
You can smell fragrances.

896
00:47:18,280 --> 00:47:20,000
You can taste delicious food.

897
00:47:23,559 --> 00:47:24,920
Chongqing hot pot,

898
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:25,840
Malatang,

899
00:47:26,239 --> 00:47:27,400
Ants climbing a tree,

900
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:29,280
Squirrel mandarin fish,

901
00:47:29,760 --> 00:47:30,920
Grilled meat skewers,

902
00:47:31,320 --> 00:47:33,199
Mapo tofu with rice,

903
00:47:34,599 --> 00:47:35,639
Braised pork,

904
00:47:36,480 --> 00:47:37,800
Stir-fried pork with chili,

905
00:47:38,639 --> 00:47:40,000
Chicken stew with mushrooms.

906
00:47:41,880 --> 00:47:43,280
You can also feel

907
00:47:44,440 --> 00:47:45,400
happiness,

908
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:46,800
anger,

909
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:48,039
sadness,

910
00:47:48,920 --> 00:47:52,199
family, friendship, love,

911
00:47:53,800 --> 00:47:55,199
and all kinds of emotions.

912
00:49:17,440 --> 00:49:19,159
My friend's restaurant,

913
00:49:19,360 --> 00:49:20,840
Success Restaurant,

914
00:49:20,840 --> 00:49:22,239
is reopening!

915
00:49:22,480 --> 00:49:25,360
Come on over and give it a try!

916
00:50:27,440 --> 00:50:28,880
I'm telling you, this place is super popular.

917
00:50:29,159 --> 00:50:30,199
Just look at that line.

918
00:50:30,519 --> 00:50:31,519
If Old Wang and the guys hadn't come early,

919
00:50:31,519 --> 00:50:32,760
I swear we'd be waiting forever.

920
00:50:32,760 --> 00:50:33,440
Bie Fan!

921
00:50:33,960 --> 00:50:35,039
Order's up!

922
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:41,159
Move it, Bie Fan! Hustle, hustle, hustle!

923
00:50:45,920 --> 00:50:47,280
Sorry for the wait. We're packed today.

924
00:50:47,679 --> 00:50:49,039
Please take a number.

925
00:50:49,039 --> 00:50:50,360
Step up when called. Here.

926
00:50:50,360 --> 00:50:51,559
Here, here. Okay.

927
00:50:52,480 --> 00:50:53,760
Okay, here, here. Take it.

928
00:50:54,559 --> 00:50:55,719
Anyone here need one? Over here. Here.

929
00:50:56,280 --> 00:50:57,280
Okay, here. I'll write one right now. Here.

930
00:50:57,360 --> 00:50:58,960
You're forty-nine. Here.

931
00:50:59,079 --> 00:51:00,360
Okay, okay, okay.

932
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:02,320
Need to take one here too. Okay.

933
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:03,880
We'll start with Mapo Tofu.

934
00:51:04,800 --> 00:51:06,239
Are you Master Bie?

935
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:07,440
I'm your fan.

936
00:51:47,039 --> 00:51:47,840
Here.

937
00:51:51,239 --> 00:51:52,480
Mom! Mom!

938
00:51:53,039 --> 00:51:54,960
I don't know how to write this poem.

939
00:51:54,960 --> 00:51:56,800
Bie Fan, order up for table five!

940
00:52:00,920 --> 00:52:01,480
What are...

941
00:52:01,800 --> 00:52:03,480
What did you write here?

942
00:52:03,480 --> 00:52:04,639
What is this?

943
00:52:04,639 --> 00:52:05,440
What's wrong?

944
00:52:05,519 --> 00:52:06,559
Is it not good?

945
00:52:07,280 --> 00:52:08,480
Writing poetry, you know...

946
00:52:09,119 --> 00:52:10,400
You don't have to hold back.

947
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:11,440
Just write whatever comes to mind.

948
00:52:11,440 --> 00:52:13,039
You can just write nonsense.

949
00:52:13,480 --> 00:52:14,639
Or even make things up.

950
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:16,360
You don't have to overthink every word.

951
00:52:16,360 --> 00:52:17,079
Or make it sound all formal.

952
00:52:17,519 --> 00:52:19,400
You talk as if you know how.

953
00:52:20,280 --> 00:52:21,480
Watch your mouth.

954
00:52:22,239 --> 00:52:22,760
This kid...

955
00:52:24,280 --> 00:52:25,960
I can write poems in my sleep!

956
00:52:27,679 --> 00:52:28,760
Then let's hear one.

957
00:52:36,760 --> 00:52:39,159
This kid looks pretty neat,

958
00:52:39,760 --> 00:52:41,920
Eyes like black coal, what a treat.

959
00:52:42,280 --> 00:52:43,880
Writes essays like a total pro,

960
00:52:46,239 --> 00:52:47,840
Makes the teacher nod just so.

961
00:52:47,960 --> 00:52:48,599
Thanks.

962
00:52:48,880 --> 00:52:50,400
What did you just write?

963
00:52:51,360 --> 00:52:52,440
Call me when our number's up.

964
00:52:53,480 --> 00:52:54,320
I'm a little rusty.

965
00:52:55,639 --> 00:52:57,559
His poem was indeed a bit too casual.

966
00:52:58,119 --> 00:52:59,320
But you shouldn't be rude.

967
00:53:00,280 --> 00:53:01,159
Boss! Boss!

968
00:53:01,159 --> 00:53:01,760
Come here a sec.

969
00:53:04,639 --> 00:53:06,159
Why is this table so wobbly?

970
00:53:09,719 --> 00:53:10,239
Coming!

971
00:53:23,480 --> 00:53:24,400
A newly written book
